# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding untuk versi terbaru boson Qiskit"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-getting-started\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Bose-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities against an exact reference. What makes the route interesting is a single idea:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini membangun circuit untuk **dinamika waktu model Bose-Hubbard satu dimensi**, mulai dari menuliskan Hamiltonian sampai memeriksa densitas site hasil evolusi terhadap referensi eksak. Yang membuat jalur ini menarik adalah satu ide:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Do not choose a boson-to-qubit encoding when you build the circuit. Build the circuit on **bosonic modes**, and let the **transpiler** decide how those modes become qubits.\n"
msgstr "> Jangan memilih encoding boson-ke-qubit saat membangun circuit. Bangun circuit di atas **mode bosonik**, dan biarkan **transpiler** yang memutuskan bagaimana mode-mode itu menjadi qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For bosons, you nearly always need to defer the encoding. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional and no encoding exists until you first pick a **truncation** $d$ (the number of occupation levels you keep). In code the truncation is given as the largest occupation a mode can hold, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, so a mode that keeps the levels $0, 1, 2$ has `max_occupation = 2` and $d = 3$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk boson, hampir selalu kamu perlu menunda encoding. Sebuah mode bosonik bisa menampung partikel dalam jumlah berapa pun, jadi ruang Fock-nya berdimensi tak hingga dan tidak ada encoding sampai kamu memilih dulu sebuah **truncation** $d$ (jumlah level okupansi yang kamu pertahankan). Dalam kode, truncation diberikan sebagai okupansi terbesar yang bisa ditampung sebuah mode, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, jadi mode yang mempertahankan level $0, 1, 2$ punya `max_occupation = 2` dan $d = 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That makes the truncation a *parameter of the encoding*, not of the physics, and it is a parameter you want to vary: too small and the answer is wrong, too large and the circuit is needlessly wide. If you defer the encoding to transpile time, you can sweep the truncation without changing the circuit, the Hamiltonian, or the grouping.\n"
msgstr "Itu membuat truncation menjadi *parameter encoding*, bukan parameter fisika, dan parameter ini memang ingin kamu variasikan: terlalu kecil jawabannya salah, terlalu besar circuit-nya melebar tanpa perlu. Kalau kamu menunda encoding sampai waktu transpile, kamu bisa menyapu truncation tanpa mengubah circuit, Hamiltonian, atau pengelompokannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [operators guide](operators#operators-explanation) for the operator data structure, the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the encodings and the recipe for writing a custom mapper, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Lihat juga\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [Panduan operator](operators#operators-explanation) untuk struktur data operator, [panduan mapper](mappers#mappers-explanation) untuk encoding dan resep menulis mapper kustom, serta [panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) untuk tahap-tahap transpiler yang dirujuk di seluruh panduan ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncation, and what it costs {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"
msgstr "Truncation, dan biayanya {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you truncate a mode to $d$ levels, you break the canonical commutator on the highest retained level <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), so no encoding is an isomorphism of *algebras*: a bosonic encoding maps states, and operators acting within the truncated subspace. Two consequences matter for everything that follows:\n"
msgstr "Ketika kamu memotong sebuah mode menjadi $d$ level, kamu merusak komutator kanonik pada level tertinggi yang dipertahankan <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), sehingga tidak ada encoding yang merupakan isomorfisme *aljabar*: encoding bosonik memetakan state, dan operator yang bekerja di dalam subruang terpotong. Dua konsekuensi penting untuk semua yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$d$ must bound the occupation reachable by the dynamics, not merely that of the initial state.\n"
msgstr "$d$ harus membatasi okupansi yang bisa dicapai oleh dinamika, bukan hanya okupansi state awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping does not commute with normal ordering, so decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and stay consistent.\n"
msgstr "Pemetaan tidak komut dengan normal ordering, jadi putuskan sekali apakah Hamiltonian-mu didefinisikan dalam bentuk normal-ordered, lalu tetap konsisten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [mappers guide](mappers#truncation-explanation) derives the defect and shows both consequences on running code.\n"
msgstr "[Panduan mapper](mappers#truncation-explanation) menurunkan cacat tersebut dan menunjukkan kedua konsekuensi pada kode yang berjalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Bose-Hubbard model on a lattice with bonds $\\langle i j \\rangle$ is\n"
msgstr "Model Bose-Hubbard pada lattice dengan bond $\\langle i j \\rangle$ adalah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. The interaction counts *pairs* of bosons on a site, so it requires a site to hold two particles at once. Normal-ordered, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which is the form used in what follows.\n"
msgstr "dengan $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. Interaksi ini menghitung *pasangan* boson pada sebuah site, jadi sebuah site harus bisa menampung dua partikel sekaligus. Dalam bentuk normal-ordered, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, yang merupakan bentuk yang dipakai selanjutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The geometry enters only through the edge list, so nothing is specific to a chain:\n"
msgstr "Geometrinya hanya masuk lewat daftar edge, jadi tidak ada yang spesifik untuk sebuah rantai:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two properties are worth checking first. The Hamiltonian must be Hermitian for $e^{-itH}$ to be unitary, and it conserves the total boson number:\n"
msgstr "Ada dua properti yang layak dicek dulu. Hamiltonian harus Hermitian agar $e^{-itH}$ unitary, dan ia menjaga jumlah total boson tetap:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the bosonic question: how many levels does this operator demand?\n"
msgstr "Sekarang pertanyaan bosoniknya: berapa banyak level yang dituntut operator ini?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interaction term applies two creation operators to one mode, so a mode has to hold two bosons for the term to act at all. That is a **maximum occupation** of 2, which is the number that [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") takes as its `max_occupation`. A mode that keeps the occupations $0, 1, 2$ has $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ levels, so `max_occupation >= 2` is the same requirement as $d \\geq 3$.\n"
msgstr "Suku interaksi menerapkan dua operator pembentukan pada satu mode, jadi sebuah mode harus bisa menampung dua boson agar suku itu bisa bekerja sama sekali. Itu berarti **okupansi maksimum** sebesar 2, yaitu angka yang diterima [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") sebagai `max_occupation`-nya. Sebuah mode yang mempertahankan okupansi $0, 1, 2$ punya $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ level, jadi `max_occupation >= 2` adalah syarat yang sama dengan $d \\geq 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a lower bound only: it comes from one application of the operator, and repeated application over a time evolution can reach further. It rules out cutoffs that are certainly too small, and step 6 settles, for this model and state, how large the cutoff has to be. [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") reports the bound for each mode separately, which is what a per-mode cutoff is compared against.\n"
msgstr "Ini hanya batas bawah: ia berasal dari satu kali penerapan operator, dan penerapan berulang selama evolusi waktu bisa menjangkau lebih jauh. Batas ini menyingkirkan cutoff yang pasti terlalu kecil, dan langkah 6 menentukan, untuk model dan state ini, seberapa besar cutoff yang diperlukan. [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") melaporkan batas untuk tiap mode secara terpisah, yang menjadi pembanding untuk cutoff per mode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"group-before-mapping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-grouping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Group before mapping {#2-group-before-mapping}"
msgstr "2. Kelompokkan sebelum memetakan {#2-group-before-mapping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The evolution is Trotterized, and how the Hamiltonian is partitioned decides what the synthesis is handed. Two considerations pull in the same direction.\n"
msgstr "Evolusinya di-Trotterize, dan cara Hamiltonian dipartisi menentukan apa yang diserahkan ke sintesis. Dua pertimbangan mengarah ke arah yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, a physical one: the individual hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is **not Hermitian**. Only the pair $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ is. If you evolve under a single non-Hermitian term, the operation is not unitary, and the mapped operator would carry complex coefficients that [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects. Each bond’s two hopping terms must therefore stay together.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, pertimbangan fisika: suku hopping individual $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ **tidak Hermitian**. Hanya pasangan $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ yang Hermitian. Kalau kamu mengevolusikan dengan satu suku non-Hermitian, operasinya tidak unitary, dan operator terpetakan akan membawa koefisien kompleks yang ditolak oleh [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). Karena itu, dua suku hopping dari tiap bond harus tetap bersama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, an efficiency one: all the on-site interaction terms are diagonal in the occupation basis and mutually commute, so they can share a single group and be synthesized together. The same holds for the bonds that touch no common site. On a chain, every second bond is such a set: bonds 0 and 2 act on disjoint pairs of modes, so their hopping terms commute and can share a group, and bond 1 forms a group of its own. If you group the even and the odd bonds, you therefore need three groups, where one group per bond needs four. Fewer groups mean fewer factors, and also a shallower circuit: with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2` the two-qubit depth is 95 against 139. The lattice decides which bonds can share a group, which is why the partition is chosen here.\n"
msgstr "Kedua, pertimbangan efisiensi: semua suku interaksi on-site bersifat diagonal pada basis okupansi dan saling komut, jadi mereka bisa berbagi satu grup dan disintesis bersama. Hal yang sama berlaku untuk bond yang tidak menyentuh site yang sama. Pada rantai, setiap bond kedua membentuk himpunan seperti itu: bond 0 dan 2 bekerja pada pasangan mode yang saling lepas, jadi suku hopping mereka komut dan bisa berbagi satu grup, sedangkan bond 1 membentuk grupnya sendiri. Kalau kamu mengelompokkan bond genap dan ganjil, kamu hanya butuh tiga grup, sementara satu grup per bond butuh empat. Grup yang lebih sedikit berarti faktor yang lebih sedikit, dan juga circuit yang lebih dangkal: dengan Gray code pada `max_occupation = 2`, depth dua-qubit-nya 95 berbanding 139. Lattice menentukan bond mana yang bisa berbagi grup, itulah sebabnya partisi dipilih di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute carries that decision into the circuit: an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one sub-evolution per group. The partition is chosen at the bosonic level, while the lattice structure is still visible, and it survives untouched through the mapping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) covers the checks a grouping should pass.\n"
msgstr "Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") membawa keputusan itu ke dalam circuit: gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") di atas operator yang dikelompokkan terurai menjadi satu sub-evolusi per grup. Partisi dipilih di level bosonik, selagi struktur lattice masih terlihat, dan ia bertahan utuh sepanjang pemetaan. [Panduan pengelompokan](grouping#grouping-explanation) membahas pemeriksaan yang harus lolos oleh sebuah pengelompokan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every group must itself be Hermitian, which is what the preceding pairing buys. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks all groups in one call:\n"
msgstr "Setiap grup harus Hermitian juga, dan itulah yang didapat dari pemasangan sebelumnya. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") memeriksa semua grup dalam satu panggilan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see what each group holds, separate the groups:\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat isi tiap grup, pisahkan grup-grupnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The even-and-odd grouping is a choice, and the alternative is easy to measure. If you give every bond a group of its own, you need four groups, and the same circuit then costs more two-qubit depth. The depth is counted after the circuit is lowered with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2`, which step 4 explains:\n"
msgstr "Pengelompokan genap-dan-ganjil adalah sebuah pilihan, dan alternatifnya mudah diukur. Kalau kamu memberi setiap bond grupnya sendiri, kamu butuh empat grup, dan circuit yang sama kemudian memakan depth dua-qubit lebih banyak. Depth dihitung setelah circuit diturunkan dengan Gray code pada `max_occupation = 2`, yang dijelaskan di langkah 4:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-bosonic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. The bosonic circuit {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr "3. Circuit bosonik {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note what is absent from the circuit. There is no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. It acts on four bosonic modes:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan apa yang tidak ada di circuit ini. Tidak ada truncation, tidak ada encoding, dan tidak ada jumlah qubit. Circuit ini bekerja pada empat mode bosonik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The wires are bosonic modes, not qubits. Note that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") takes **integers**, not flags: a mode can hold any number of bosons, so a Fock state is a list of occupation numbers.\n"
msgstr "Kabel-kabelnya adalah mode bosonik, bukan qubit. Perhatikan bahwa [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") menerima **bilangan bulat**, bukan flag: sebuah mode bisa menampung boson dalam jumlah berapa pun, jadi state Fock adalah daftar bilangan okupansi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") turns the grouping from [step 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping) into one gate per group:\n"
msgstr "Satu kali [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") mengubah pengelompokan dari [langkah 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping) menjadi satu gate per grup:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first group holds the bonds on modes 0 and 1 and on modes 2 and 3, so its gate spans all four modes, and so does the on-site group. The middle bond has a gate of its own on modes 1 and 2.\n"
msgstr "Grup pertama memuat bond pada mode 0 dan 1 serta pada mode 2 dan 3, jadi gate-nya mencakup keempat mode, begitu juga grup on-site. Bond tengah punya gate sendiri pada mode 1 dan 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Skip that decomposition and the grouping is simply ignored. Which method does the splitting is the `synthesis` of the gate, with [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") as the default; [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows the alternatives.\n"
msgstr "Lewati dekomposisi itu dan pengelompokan akan diabaikan begitu saja. Metode yang melakukan pemecahan adalah `synthesis` dari gate, dengan [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") sebagai default-nya; [Sintesis gate Evolution di ruang bosonik](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) menunjukkan alternatifnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Choose the encoding at transpile time {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"
msgstr "4. Pilih encoding saat waktu transpile {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the payoff. The same circuit is lowered four times, under four different [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") values, by changing one argument. A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") pairs the encoding with the truncation of every mode, and the following preset derives the layout, the state preparation, and the operator mapping from that one spec (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). A string such as `\"gray\"` is accepted wherever a `LevelEncoding` is.\n"
msgstr "Inilah hasilnya. Circuit yang sama diturunkan empat kali, dengan empat nilai [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") berbeda, hanya dengan mengubah satu argumen. Sebuah [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") memasangkan encoding dengan truncation setiap mode, dan preset berikut menurunkan layout, persiapan state, dan pemetaan operator dari satu spec itu (lihat [Menjelaskan truncation dengan LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). String seperti `\"gray\"` diterima di mana pun sebuah `LevelEncoding` diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These numbers contradict a natural guess. The unary encodings use $d$ qubits per mode against $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ for the compact codes, and at $d = 3$ the compact codes win on both axes at once: fewer qubits and far fewer entangling gates. The two unary variants differ in the operator they emit, not in their layout: [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") carries a projector on every other qubit of a mode, which makes it the most expensive of the four to evolve, and [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") leaves the projectors out and agrees with it on the one-hot subspace. The [mappers guide](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) shows the two operators side by side, and explains why the Gray code beats standard binary (SB) on the hopping terms.\n"
msgstr "Angka-angka ini bertentangan dengan tebakan yang wajar. Encoding unary memakai $d$ qubit per mode, dibandingkan $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ untuk kode kompak, dan pada $d = 3$ kode kompak menang di kedua sisi sekaligus: qubit lebih sedikit dan gate entangling jauh lebih sedikit. Kedua varian unary berbeda pada operator yang mereka hasilkan, bukan pada layout-nya: [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") membawa proyektor pada setiap qubit selang-seling dalam sebuah mode, yang membuatnya paling mahal untuk dievolusikan di antara keempatnya, dan [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") menghilangkan proyektor dan sepakat dengannya pada subruang one-hot. [Panduan mapper](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) menampilkan kedua operator berdampingan, dan menjelaskan kenapa Gray code mengalahkan standard binary (SB) pada suku hopping.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sawaya et al. report the same ordering <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"
msgstr "Sawaya et al. melaporkan urutan yang sama <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> though the unary code tends to require more qubits but fewer operations, it is often the case that the SB or Gray code is more efficient both in terms of qubit counts and operation counts\n"
msgstr "> meskipun kode unary cenderung membutuhkan lebih banyak qubit tetapi lebih sedikit operasi, sering kali kode SB atau Gray lebih efisien, baik dari sisi jumlah qubit maupun jumlah operasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Their conclusion is that the best code depends on the Hamiltonian and on $d$, which is the strongest argument for not fixing the choice in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kesimpulan mereka adalah bahwa kode terbaik bergantung pada Hamiltonian dan pada $d$, dan itu argumen terkuat untuk tidak mengunci pilihan di dalam circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Under a level encoding a mode spans several qubits, so the qubit register is wider than the mode register. The preset uses [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), which derives the register width from the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) walks through the stages the preset runs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Di bawah level encoding, sebuah mode mencakup beberapa qubit, jadi register qubit lebih lebar daripada register mode. Preset memakai [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), yang menurunkan lebar register dari [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). [Panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) menelusuri tahap-tahap yang dijalankan preset.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-against-exact-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Verify against exact dynamics {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"
msgstr "5. Verifikasi terhadap dinamika eksak {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "None of the preceding steps establishes that the circuit is right. For that, compare the site densities $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ after evolution against an exact reference computed on the encoded Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Tidak ada langkah sebelumnya yang membuktikan bahwa circuit-nya benar. Untuk itu, bandingkan densitas site $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ setelah evolusi dengan referensi eksak yang dihitung pada Hamiltonian terenkode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference has to be computed in the same truncated space the circuit works in, because comparing against an untruncated calculation would conflate Trotter error with truncation error, which are different things and worth separating (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Referensi harus dihitung di ruang terpotong yang sama dengan tempat circuit bekerja, karena membandingkan dengan perhitungan tanpa truncation akan mencampur error Trotter dengan error truncation, yang merupakan dua hal berbeda dan layak dipisahkan (lihat [Memotong ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With those in hand, the exact evolution in the truncated space:\n"
msgstr "Dengan semua itu di tangan, berikut evolusi eksak di ruang terpotong:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bosons spread from the occupied end of the chain towards the empty one, and the two bosons are conserved:\n"
msgstr "Boson menyebar dari ujung rantai yang terisi menuju ujung yang kosong, dan kedua boson tetap terjaga:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the circuit. Note that the preceding reference was built from `initial` directly, so the circuit compared against it must contain only the evolution, because the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate would re-prepare a state that is already prepared.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang circuit-nya. Perhatikan bahwa referensi sebelumnya dibangun langsung dari `initial`, jadi circuit yang dibandingkan dengannya harus hanya berisi evolusi, karena gate [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") akan menyiapkan ulang state yang sudah disiapkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error halves as the step count doubles, which is the $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ signature of a first-order product formula. That is the evidence that the discrepancy is Trotter error and the encoding is faithful.\n"
msgstr "Error-nya turun setengah ketika jumlah langkah digandakan, yang merupakan ciri khas $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ dari product formula orde pertama. Itu bukti bahwa selisihnya adalah error Trotter dan encoding-nya setia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The repetitions come from the `synthesis` of the gate, which Trotterizes in bosonic space where the grouping still exists: each step applies every group once, and the steps follow one another. That is different from handing a [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) with `reps > 1` to the qubit-level synthesis plugin. There, each group is already its own [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), so the formula only subdivides the terms within a group and never interleaves the groups. The groups do not mutually commute, so that leaves a single outer Trotter step whose error does not shrink however large `reps` is. [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) compares the two and covers higher orders.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Pengulangan berasal dari `synthesis` gate, yang melakukan Trotterize di ruang bosonik tempat pengelompokan masih ada: setiap langkah menerapkan setiap grup sekali, dan langkah-langkahnya berurutan. Itu berbeda dengan memberikan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) dengan `reps > 1` ke plugin sintesis tingkat qubit. Di sana, setiap grup sudah menjadi [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) sendiri, sehingga formula hanya membagi suku-suku di dalam satu grup dan tidak pernah menyisipkan grup-grup secara bergantian. Grup-grup itu tidak saling komut, jadi yang tersisa adalah satu langkah Trotter luar yang error-nya tidak mengecil sebesar apa pun `reps`. [Sintesis gate Evolution di ruang bosonik](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) membandingkan keduanya dan membahas orde yang lebih tinggi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The preceding [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) call is essential. [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) uses a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s exact definition and bypasses the product formula entirely. If you verify against an un-decomposed circuit, you see near-perfect agreement even for a deliberately wrong synthesis. The un-decomposed circuit also forces a dense $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$ operator to be built, whereas a decomposed circuit applies gates one at a time. Other simulators can treat the gate differently, so this check depends on the simulator, whereas hardware always needs the decomposed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Peringatan\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Pemanggilan [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) sebelumnya itu penting. [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) memakai definisi eksak dari [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) dan melewati product formula sepenuhnya. Kalau kamu memverifikasi terhadap circuit yang belum didekomposisi, kamu akan melihat kecocokan nyaris sempurna bahkan untuk sintesis yang sengaja dibuat salah. Circuit yang belum didekomposisi juga memaksa pembangunan operator padat $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$, sedangkan circuit yang didekomposisi menerapkan gate satu per satu. Simulator lain bisa memperlakukan gate secara berbeda, jadi pemeriksaan ini bergantung pada simulator, sedangkan hardware selalu butuh bentuk yang didekomposisi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the central check: the physics must not depend on which encoding was chosen.\n"
msgstr "Terakhir, pemeriksaan utama: fisikanya tidak boleh bergantung pada encoding yang dipilih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qubit counts, Pauli structures, and circuit depths all differ, and the physics agrees to ten decimal places. The encoding is an implementation choice, which is why it belongs to the transpiler. The two unary variants agree here because the simulated state stays on the one-hot subspace; away from it they would differ.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah qubit, struktur Pauli, dan depth circuit semuanya berbeda, dan fisikanya cocok sampai sepuluh angka desimal. Encoding adalah pilihan implementasi, itulah kenapa ia menjadi urusan transpiler. Kedua varian unary cocok di sini karena state yang disimulasikan tetap berada di subruang one-hot; di luar itu keduanya akan berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Truncation is a convergence parameter {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"
msgstr "6. Truncation adalah parameter konvergensi {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final step is specific to bosons. Everything so far had fixed `max_occupation = 2`, that is $d = 3$. However, the truncation is not a free choice: it is a **convergence parameter**, and an answer is only trustworthy after it stops moving (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Langkah terakhir ini spesifik untuk boson. Sejauh ini semuanya memakai `max_occupation = 2` yang tetap, yaitu $d = 3$. Namun, truncation bukan pilihan bebas: ia adalah **parameter konvergensi**, dan sebuah jawaban baru bisa dipercaya setelah ia berhenti bergerak (lihat [Memotong ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit carries no truncation, so the circuit itself does not change when the cutoff does: only the transpilation is repeated. What changes is the size of what comes out, and a sweep is only as cheap as it is here because the system is tiny. The following reference is an exact classical simulation of the truncated dynamics, which is possible for four sites and grows exponentially with the number of qubits. For a problem beyond that reach there is no exact reference to compare against, and the convergence has to be judged by other means.\n"
msgstr "Circuit tidak membawa truncation, jadi circuit itu sendiri tidak berubah ketika cutoff berubah: hanya transpilasinya yang diulang. Yang berubah adalah ukuran hasilnya, dan sapuan seperti ini hanya semurah di sini karena sistemnya sangat kecil. Referensi berikut adalah simulasi klasik eksak dari dinamika terpotong, yang mungkin dilakukan untuk empat site dan tumbuh secara eksponensial terhadap jumlah qubit. Untuk masalah di luar jangkauan itu, tidak ada referensi eksak untuk dibandingkan, dan konvergensinya harus dinilai dengan cara lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$) each site holds at most one boson, so the interaction term, which needs two on a site, cannot act at all, and the densities are off by about $7 \\times 10^{-4}$. When you add the third level, the result captures the interaction, and from `max_occupation = 3` on the result is stationary to machine precision: converged.\n"
msgstr "Pada `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$) setiap site menampung paling banyak satu boson, sehingga suku interaksi, yang butuh dua boson pada satu site, sama sekali tidak bisa bekerja, dan densitasnya meleset sekitar $7 \\times 10^{-4}$. Ketika kamu menambahkan level ketiga, hasilnya menangkap interaksi, dan mulai dari `max_occupation = 3` hasilnya stasioner sampai presisi mesin: sudah konvergen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reason that it stops at `max_occupation = 2` is particle number. The Hamiltonian conserves the number of bosons, and this state holds two, so no site can ever hold more than two, whatever the evolution time and whether the interaction is repulsive or attractive. If you evolve to $t = 6$ instead of $t = 0.4$, or flip the sign of $U$, the densities at `max_occupation = 2` and higher stay unchanged to $10^{-13}$.\n"
msgstr "Alasan ia berhenti di `max_occupation = 2` adalah jumlah partikel. Hamiltonian menjaga jumlah boson, dan state ini memuat dua, jadi tidak ada site yang pernah bisa menampung lebih dari dua, berapa pun waktu evolusinya dan baik interaksinya tolak-menolak maupun tarik-menarik. Kalau kamu mengevolusikan sampai $t = 6$ alih-alih $t = 0.4$, atau membalik tanda $U$, densitas pada `max_occupation = 2` dan lebih tinggi tetap tidak berubah sampai $10^{-13}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does push the requirement up is the **number of bosons**. Three bosons on the same chain change by about $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ between `max_occupation = 2` and `3` after the same short evolution, and by about $0.3$ after $t = 6$. That is a statement about this model and a conserved quantity, and it is a bound only for operators that conserve the particle number; it is not a general rule, so the cutoff has to be swept, not guessed.\n"
msgstr "Yang justru menaikkan kebutuhan adalah **jumlah boson**. Tiga boson pada rantai yang sama berubah sekitar $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ antara `max_occupation = 2` dan `3` setelah evolusi pendek yang sama, dan sekitar $0.3$ setelah $t = 6$. Itu pernyataan tentang model ini dan satu besaran terjaga, dan ia hanya batas untuk operator yang menjaga jumlah partikel; itu bukan aturan umum, jadi cutoff harus disapu, bukan ditebak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sweep has a price on the circuit side too, which is what the exact reference does not show. The same bosonic circuit, lowered with the Gray code at each cutoff:\n"
msgstr "Sapuan ini punya harga di sisi circuit juga, yang tidak ditunjukkan oleh referensi eksak. Circuit bosonik yang sama, diturunkan dengan Gray code pada tiap cutoff:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each extra level costs depth, and the qubit count jumps whenever $d$ passes a power of two. When you converge in $d$, you therefore trade accuracy against circuit size, so the sweep is more than a numerical check.\n"
msgstr "Setiap level tambahan menambah depth, dan jumlah qubit melonjak setiap kali $d$ melewati pangkat dua. Ketika kamu mengonvergenkan $d$, kamu jadi menukar akurasi dengan ukuran circuit, jadi sapuan ini lebih dari sekadar pemeriksaan numerik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that $d = 2$ being nearly right is a coincidence of the observable: the site *densities* barely move, while the underlying state is qualitatively wrong (it has no doubly-occupied component). If one observable converges, that does not show that another has converged.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan juga bahwa $d = 2$ yang hampir benar hanyalah kebetulan dari observabelnya: *densitas* site nyaris tidak bergerak, sementara state yang mendasarinya salah secara kualitatif (tidak punya komponen yang terisi ganda). Kalau satu observabel konvergen, itu tidak menunjukkan bahwa observabel lain sudah konvergen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Yang perlu dibawa pulang {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The encoding is a transpiler concern.** The bosonic circuit in [step 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile) mentions no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. Four encodings then lowered it to four different circuits, all reproducing the same physics. Nothing upstream of the transpiler had to change.\n"
msgstr "**Encoding adalah urusan transpiler.** Circuit bosonik di [langkah 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile) tidak menyebut truncation, encoding, ataupun jumlah qubit. Empat encoding lalu menurunkannya menjadi empat circuit berbeda, dan semuanya menghasilkan fisika yang sama. Tidak ada yang perlu diubah di bagian hulu transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**For bosons this is not merely convenient.** The truncation is a convergence parameter that has to be swept, and it lives inside the encoding. A circuit built against a fixed encoding would have to be rebuilt for every value of $d$.\n"
msgstr "**Untuk boson, ini bukan sekadar kenyamanan.** Truncation adalah parameter konvergensi yang harus disapu (sweep), dan letaknya di dalam encoding. Circuit yang dibangun terhadap encoding tetap harus dibangun ulang untuk setiap nilai $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping, and group for Hermiticity.** A single hopping term is not Hermitian and cannot be exponentiated; the bond pair on the hand is Hermitian and therefore can be exponentiated. Decide the partition at the bosonic level, where the lattice is still visible. That is physically necessary, and the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute exists to carry the decision forward.\n"
msgstr "**Kelompokkan sebelum mapping, dan kelompokkan demi Hermitisitas.** Satu suku hopping tidak Hermitian dan tidak bisa dieksponensialkan; pasangan bond di sisi lain bersifat Hermitian sehingga bisa dieksponensialkan. Tentukan partisinya di level bosonik, saat kisi (lattice) masih terlihat. Itu perlu secara fisika, dan atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") ada untuk membawa keputusan itu ke tahap berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Do not assume the low-weight encoding is the cheap one.** At $d = 3$ the compact codes beat both unary variants on qubits and gates simultaneously, and the projected variant is the costliest of all. Measure; the crossover is $d$-dependent.\n"
msgstr "**Jangan berasumsi encoding berbobot rendah itu yang murah.** Pada $d = 3$ kode kompak mengalahkan kedua varian unary sekaligus dalam jumlah qubit dan gate, dan varian terproyeksi adalah yang paling mahal dari semuanya. Ukur sendiri; titik silangnya bergantung pada $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Truncation breaks the algebra, in a quantifiable way.** Only on the top retained level, by $d$. That is also why mapping does not commute with normal ordering.\n"
msgstr "**Truncation merusak aljabar, dengan cara yang bisa dikuantifikasi.** Hanya pada level teratas yang dipertahankan, sebesar $d$. Itu juga alasan mapping tidak komut dengan normal ordering.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah berikutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend this example. If you replace the chain’s edge list with the bonds of a square lattice, you need no other change, because the `bose_hubbard` function defined earlier is already geometry-agnostic. A custom encoding of your own (a block-unary code, for example, which interpolates between unary and compact) also plugs in through the same `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` seam the preset uses.\n"
msgstr "Dua arah bisa memperluas contoh ini. Kalau kamu mengganti daftar edge rantai dengan bond kisi persegi, tidak ada perubahan lain yang dibutuhkan, karena fungsi `bose_hubbard` yang didefinisikan sebelumnya sudah agnostik terhadap geometri. Encoding buatanmu sendiri (misalnya kode block-unary, yang menginterpolasi antara unary dan kompak) juga bisa dipasang lewat seam `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` yang sama dengan yang dipakai preset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
